From a42e0f63762175bdf3c67e5fbc18cc75451a9654 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:50:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Killzone port on v0.18.0: our Vulkan backend on the new
 engine interface; SPU fast float on x86

rsx_vulkan_backend.c is kz-perf-ppu's (two frames in flight, display modes, internal scale, crop/stretch, dumps), with texture_upload_ordered set, depth_packed unhooked (the engine dropped it) and shims for the host's split present. The coherence bitmap is read through upstream's spu_coh_line_reserved. SPU_FAST_FLOAT runs under MXCSR round toward zero (g_spu_float_mode): upstream's SPU_FLOAT_RZ is arm64 only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
